WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.060
[Upbeat music] Print Screen. One key. That's all it takes.

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:06.280
Capture. Annotate. Record. Share.

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:08.620
Stackshot: capture, annotate and share in seconds.

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:15.910
Seven ways to capture, one shortcut each: area, screen, window, scrolling, video, GIF and Markdown.

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:23.920
Select. Snap. Done. The capture waits in the corner as a thumbnail, ready to drag or paste with Ctrl+V.

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:31.340
Mark it up: arrows, shapes, numbered steps, text, highlight and redaction, then a presentation backdrop.

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:38.460
Hide it before you share it: one click finds IDs, IBANs, cards, e-mails and phone numbers, and covers them.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:43.870
Capture the whole page: scroll yourself, or let Stackshot scroll, into one seamless image.

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:50.790
Record your screen with sound: MP4 or GIF at up to 60 fps, with an optional webcam. Trim it, speed it up, share it.

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:57.910
Record like a pro: pause and resume, show clicks and shortcuts, and test the microphone first.

00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:04.430
Find it by what it said: search the text inside captures, read with Windows' own OCR on the PC.

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:11.550
XML and Markdown, upgraded: compare two XMLs, read SOAP at a glance, export Markdown to PDF.

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:16.700
One window, your way: three home views and every setting in one place.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:22.550
Meet Pixel, the capture sidekick, with 39 costumes.

00:01:22.550 --> 00:01:28.270
And so much more: the small things, all in the same 2.2 MB.

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:32.470
Small. Fast. Private. One 2.2 MB executable, no admin rights, no accounts, cloud or telemetry.

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:37.933
Stackshot. Free for Windows 10 and 11. Open source (MIT), no account, no telemetry. [Music ends]
